      "claim": "L5 gut-wall/efflux records do not provide query-specific affirmative low-F evidence: C49 (sulpiride P-gp efflux) and C57 (GL-V9 extensive liver metabolism) are mechanistically suggestive but structurally distant and unquantified for the query, while C51/C52/C56 show high permeability or no significant efflux for other compounds.",
      "card_ids": ["C49","C57","C51","C52","C56"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The qualitative 'low' ebastine card C23 conflicts with C02 (~40%) and C18 ('highly bioavailable') and is not threshold-relevant to the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C23","C02","C18"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "gut_wall_efflux_intestinal_metabolism",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C50","C49","C57","C51","C52","C56","C53"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct same-molecule absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the query.",
    "No query-specific Caco-2 permeability, P-gp efflux, or intestinal metabolism data; L5 records are for other molecules.",
    "Mosapride AUC (C24) lacks an IV comparator, so it cannot quantify F.",
    "The query's piperidine/propoxy-4-fluorophenyl substituent may alter permeability and first-pass handling relative to metoclopramide/mosapride.",
    "Primary aromatic amine and O-demethylation metabolic fate not experimentally assessed.",
    "Gold-context transfer is indirect and structurally diverse."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L5 adds metoclopramide high-permeability evidence and some non-query-specific efflux/metabolism concerns; no affirmative threshold-relevant low-F evidence appears. The high prediction is retained with moderate confidence."
}

